# ConnectorSuite ticket and chat session folders

**Mandatory at the start of every chat** in ConnectorSuite: pick or create **one flat folder** under `tickets/` and keep its docs current. **No date subfolders.**

## One folder per topic (flat)

| Chat type | Folder (single level under `tickets/`) |
|-----------|----------------------------------------|
| **Jira ticket** | Reuse existing workspace if present (e.g. `tickets/DCOMS-29691-pod2dev-ec2-shutdown-restart-validation/`). Otherwise `tickets/<TICKET-KEY> - <short-kebab-summary>/` |
| **Non-ticket** | `tickets/RANDOM/<task-kebab-summary>/` |

Dates belong **in file content**, not in the directory tree.

## Two files (simple split)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **`README.md`** | Stable overview: intent, status, links, artifacts, decisions, open questions. Update when those change. |
| **`CHAT-LOG.md`** | Append-only trail of chats. **New chat = new top section** (newest first). |

If a ticket workspace already has a rich `README.md` (epic docs), add **`CHAT-LOG.md`** beside it for Cursor sessions; do not duplicate the epic README.

### CHAT-LOG.md section template (per chat)

```markdown
## 2026-09-19 — <one-line title>

**Status when closed:** done | in progress | blocked | parked

- What we did (bullets)
- Files touched (paths)
```

Rename `RANDOM/...` folders when a better title is obvious; note renames at the top of `README.md` under **Previous names**.

## When to create vs reuse

- **First turn, new chat:** create the folder only if none exists for that ticket/topic; always add a new `CHAT-LOG.md` section for **this** chat.
- **Same chat:** keep editing the same `CHAT-LOG.md` section (do not add a second section for the same conversation).

## Durable work

Scripts, runbooks, and ticket docs stay in the ticket workspace. Reference them from `CHAT-LOG.md`; do not bury runbooks inside chat-only folders.

## Path hygiene

After moving or renaming under `tickets/`, search ConnectorSuite for old paths and fix `AGENTS.md`, runbooks, and absolute `C:\PROD\ConnectorSuite\...` references.
